From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: istore-ai <istoreai@istoreos.com>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 19:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost/devfreq: handle OPP pre-configured by platform code

On Rockchip platforms, rockchip_opp_select populates GPU OPP config
(regulators, supported-hw, OPP table) via the newer dev_pm_opp_set_config()
API before panfrost probes. This clashes with panfrost's use of the older
devm_pm_opp_set_regulators() API:

  - set_regulators() returns -EBUSY  (regulators already configured)
  - of_add_table()   returns -EEXIST (table already parsed)
                    or -ENOENT  (no OPPs match pre-set supported-hw)

Treat these as non-fatal:

  -EBUSY  -> skip regulator setup (already done)
  -EEXIST -> skip OPP table parsing (already done), reuse existing
  -ENOENT -> no matching OPPs, continue without devfreq (GPU runs at
             default clock; DVFS disabled)

Without this fix, panfrost probe fails with -EBUSY or -ENOENT on
RK3568/EasePi R1 running iStoreOS.

Signed-off-by: istore-ai <istoreai@istoreos.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c
index 57ae3895ef82..15147999f8df 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c
@@ -134,19 +134,29 @@ int panfrost_devfreq_init(struct panfrost_device *pfdev)
 
 	ret = devm_pm_opp_set_regulators(dev, pfdev->comp->supply_names);
 	if (ret) {
-		/* Continue if the optional regulator is missing */
-		if (ret != -ENODEV) {
+		if (ret == -EBUSY) {
+			/* Already configured by platform (rockchip_opp_select) */
+			dev_info(dev, "OPP already configured, skip set_regulators\n");
+			goto opp_add_table;
+		}
+		if (ret != -ENODEV) {
 			if (ret != -EPROBE_DEFER)
 				DRM_DEV_ERROR(dev, "Couldn't set OPP regulators\n");
 			return ret;
 		}
+		/* -ENODEV: optional regulator missing, continue */
 	}
 
+opp_add_table:
 	ret = devm_pm_opp_of_add_table(dev);
 	if (ret) {
-		/* Optional, continue without devfreq */
-		if (ret == -ENODEV)
-			ret = 0;
-		return ret;
+		if (ret == -EEXIST)
+			dev_info(dev, "OPP table already populated, continuing\n");
+		else if (ret == -ENODEV || ret == -ENOENT)
+			/* No OPP table / no supported OPPs -> continue w/o devfreq */
+			return 0;
+		else
+			return ret;
 	}
 	pfdevfreq->opp_of_table_added = true;
 
-- 
